WEBVTT

00:00:23.457 --> 00:00:27.505
&lt;i&gt;Captain's log, stardate 58496.1.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:27.548 --> 00:00:29.768
&lt;i&gt;While the primary mission
of the California-class&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:31.683
&lt;i&gt;is second contact,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:31.726 --> 00:00:35.078
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet has never considered
our work a top priority.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:37.080
&lt;i&gt;Until today.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:37.123 --> 00:00:40.779
&lt;i&gt;I'm thrilled to log that my
planetary follow-up initiative&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:44.391
&lt;i&gt;has finally been given the green
light by Admiral Buenamigo.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:44.435 --> 00:00:46.219
&lt;i&gt;Congratulations,
Captain Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:49.179
&lt;i&gt;There's no one better suited
for Project Swing By.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:52.269
And there's no one better suited
to assign it to me, Admiral.

00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:55.402
&lt;i&gt;Let's ditch the pomp and
set this conversation to facts.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:55.446 --> 00:00:57.796
"Ditch the pomp"?

00:00:57.839 --> 00:00:59.928
&lt;i&gt;The first Project Swing By
planet you'll be checking in on&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:01.539
&lt;i&gt;is Ornara.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:01.582 --> 00:01:04.629
Ornara. Picard made
first contact there, right?

00:01:04.672 --> 00:01:06.544
&lt;i&gt;Yes. 17 years ago.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:06.587 --> 00:01:08.633
&lt;i&gt;So they're long overdue
for some Starfleet attention.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:11.897
&lt;i&gt;If this goes well, Swing By
missions will be assigned&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.334
&lt;i&gt;across the entire
California-class.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:14.378 --> 00:01:17.250
Then I'll make sure
it goes better than well.

00:01:17.294 --> 00:01:20.166
&lt;i&gt;I know you will. Which is why
I have a journalist from FNN&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.037
&lt;i&gt;en route to the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.518
&lt;i&gt;She'll be documenting
your success as it happens.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:24.562 --> 00:01:26.303
&lt;i&gt;Buenamigo out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:28.435
Congratulations, Captain.
I think I speak for all of us

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.437
- when I say...
- This is terrible!

00:01:30.481 --> 00:01:33.788
But you've been lobbying
for Project Swing By for years.

00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:35.181
Not that. The reporter.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:36.704
The ship's a mess.

00:01:36.748 --> 00:01:38.228
We have to clean it up
before she gets here.

00:01:38.271 --> 00:01:39.794
Clean it up.

00:01:39.838 --> 00:01:40.969
- Good one, Captain.
- Why are you laughing?!

00:01:41.013 --> 00:01:42.406
Oh, [bleep]. She's serious.

00:01:42.449 --> 00:01:43.972
Go get your departments
in order now!

00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:46.323
- Go!
- Yes, Captain!

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.106
What do we know
about the Ornarans?

00:03:14.149 --> 00:03:16.151
They were ravaged by a plague,

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.502
the cure for which was
a plant called felicium,

00:03:18.545 --> 00:03:20.678
which only grew
on their sister planet, Brekka.

00:03:20.721 --> 00:03:22.810
The Brekkians exploited access
to the drug

00:03:22.854 --> 00:03:24.464
and got the Ornarans
hooked on it,

00:03:24.508 --> 00:03:26.466
even after the plague was cured.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.902
Some sister.

00:03:27.946 --> 00:03:29.513
What did Picard
have to say about it?

00:03:29.556 --> 00:03:31.297
By the time
the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt; got there,

00:03:31.341 --> 00:03:33.386
Ornara was in shambles
due to their addiction.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:36.476
Picard severed communication
between the planets and, uh...

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.477
well, let's see--

00:03:37.521 --> 00:03:38.739
oh, uh, then he left.

00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:40.785
- He left?
- Yeah, that's, uh...

00:03:40.828 --> 00:03:43.004
- Whew, that's how it went down.
- Seriously?

00:03:43.048 --> 00:03:45.790
So now it's our job
to check in on an entire planet

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:47.705
that Picard left cold turkey?

00:03:47.748 --> 00:03:49.359
Well, Captain,
think about it like this--

00:03:49.402 --> 00:03:51.665
if they've relapsed,
we'll provide much-needed aid.

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:54.059
Project Swing By
is gonna look great.

00:03:54.102 --> 00:03:55.408
With this reporter
coming on board,

00:03:55.452 --> 00:03:56.975
I don't want us
to look like fools.

00:03:59.064 --> 00:04:01.066
Mariner. What the hell
are you covered in?!

00:04:01.109 --> 00:04:02.676
Blueberry filling.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.374
Yeah, we got the pie eating
contest later today.

00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:05.984
Hey, we should get
that reporter to cover it.

00:04:06.027 --> 00:04:08.291
We're gonna crush Ops this year.

00:04:10.293 --> 00:04:11.337
What's her problem?

00:04:11.381 --> 00:04:12.817
We did strawberry last year.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:14.558
She doesn't always
get to pick the pie.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.734
Ensign, if I were you,
I would make myself scarce

00:04:16.777 --> 00:04:18.083
for the next couple days.

00:04:18.126 --> 00:04:19.345
Please, reporters love me.

00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:20.607
Plus, I'm so good at my job,

00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:21.782
I'm like a second captain.

00:04:21.826 --> 00:04:23.131
Yeah, I'm like a mini captain.

00:04:23.175 --> 00:04:25.003
Like a little,
sweet baby captain.

00:04:26.526 --> 00:04:27.875
We may want to roll out
some duty changes,

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:30.487
to make a good first impression.
You get me?

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.054
You better be ready to shovel
some [bleep]ing pie, Marty.

00:04:33.098 --> 00:04:34.926
Your whole division's
going down!

00:04:34.969 --> 00:04:37.624
Loud and clear.

00:04:37.668 --> 00:04:39.365
Gah! What the hell?

00:04:39.409 --> 00:04:41.498
Captain gave our next rotation
to alpha shift?

00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:43.674
I-I didn't even know
there was an alpha shift.

00:04:43.717 --> 00:04:45.240
We have orders to keep
our work areas spotless,

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.894
but I accidentally got
my station stuck

00:04:46.938 --> 00:04:48.287
in the transporter buffer.

00:04:48.331 --> 00:04:50.071
What if it's messy in there?

00:04:50.115 --> 00:04:52.117
I'm not allowed to scan anything
until after the reporter leaves,

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.423
but I scan when I get nervous.

00:04:53.466 --> 00:04:55.381
Hey, Carol gonna Carol, right?

00:04:55.425 --> 00:04:57.514
I mean, she's just trying to put
her best foot forward. I get it.

00:04:57.557 --> 00:05:00.038
All we got to do is sit back
and make her look great.

00:05:00.081 --> 00:05:01.996
Wow, that's weirdly
mature of you.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.347
Wow, Captain.
I have to tell you,

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:08.525
covering a California-class ship
is really special for me.

00:05:08.568 --> 00:05:10.135
My family's from Flagstaff.

00:05:10.178 --> 00:05:13.138
: Ah, yes.
Arizona is...

00:05:13.181 --> 00:05:14.748
very near California.

00:05:14.792 --> 00:05:16.533
Oh, it's just gorgeous.

00:05:16.576 --> 00:05:18.665
Victoria, let's get you settled
in those guest quarters.

00:05:18.709 --> 00:05:21.276
- Pretty great view, huh?
- Oh, it's stunning.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.843
And, you know, when it comes
to the lower decks,

00:05:22.887 --> 00:05:24.671
nobody knows it better
than beta shift.

00:05:24.715 --> 00:05:26.194
So if you want a tour
or something,

00:05:26.238 --> 00:05:28.066
- just let me know.
- Actually, Ensign,

00:05:28.109 --> 00:05:31.809
I believe your shift doesn't
begin for another three cycles.

00:05:31.852 --> 00:05:33.637
Right. That's why I have time.
I'm early.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.031
Junior officers
can be a bit excitable.

00:05:37.075 --> 00:05:40.078
You know, sometimes they forget
they should be going to bed.

00:05:40.121 --> 00:05:41.471
Computer.

00:05:41.514 --> 00:05:43.386
Lights. Have you
ever seen a warp core?

00:05:43.429 --> 00:05:45.605
Oh, my gosh, no.
But I can't wait.

00:05:45.649 --> 00:05:48.129
- Whoa, seriously?
- Well, that was demoralizing.

00:05:48.173 --> 00:05:49.870
She's just...
She's under a lot of pressure.

00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:51.698
But, hey, this-this gives us
more time to practice

00:05:51.742 --> 00:05:52.743
for the pie eating contest.

00:05:52.786 --> 00:05:54.745
Yeah!

00:05:54.788 --> 00:05:56.399
The pie eating
contest is canceled?

00:05:56.442 --> 00:05:58.792
But I've been expanding
my G.I. tract to store more pie.

00:05:58.836 --> 00:06:01.099
And I perfected
dislocating my jaw.

00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:03.623
Mariner,
what is your mom thinking?

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.233
This is the biggest crew night
of the year,

00:06:05.277 --> 00:06:06.496
not including &lt;i&gt;pon farrs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:06.539 --> 00:06:07.801
Yeah, I don't really
know what...

00:06:09.412 --> 00:06:10.761
Hey. Hey, man. No, not the pies.

00:06:10.804 --> 00:06:12.284
Hey, stop! We'll take those.

00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:14.939
Captain's orders.
No contest, no pies.

00:06:14.982 --> 00:06:16.636
Sir, I've been
starving myself for days.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.072
Please! My body needs crust!

00:06:18.116 --> 00:06:19.813
Stand back, Ensign.
I have my orders.

00:06:19.857 --> 00:06:20.858
Aw.

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:21.946
Come on, guys.

00:06:21.989 --> 00:06:23.338
There's plenty to do around here

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:24.601
that doesn't end
in sugary diarrhea.

00:06:24.644 --> 00:06:26.080
Oh. Maybe for you.

00:06:26.124 --> 00:06:27.430
Let's go grab some synthehol

00:06:27.473 --> 00:06:29.344
and synthe-have
a great time at the bar.

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:30.345
&lt;i&gt;Sir.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:31.825
Look at me. Look at me!

00:06:31.869 --> 00:06:33.740
- Please, just one!
- I can't.

00:06:33.784 --> 00:06:34.959
You know I can't.

00:06:35.002 --> 00:06:36.264
Then stun me!

00:06:36.308 --> 00:06:37.440
No!

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.095
&lt;i&gt;Don't look at
the holo-imager. Look at me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:41.139 --> 00:06:43.794
&lt;i&gt;Okay, and just tell me what life
is like on the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos.

00:06:43.837 --> 00:06:45.883
Okay. Is this good?

00:06:45.926 --> 00:06:47.798
Last week,
I got to scan an ancient probe

00:06:47.841 --> 00:06:49.234
from an unknown civilization,

00:06:49.277 --> 00:06:52.280
and I just signed up
for aerial silks.

00:06:52.324 --> 00:06:56.154
For me, the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is life
in the cave of Garanoga.

00:06:56.197 --> 00:06:58.243
Oh, you poor thing.
They make you live in a cave?

00:06:58.286 --> 00:07:00.158
: No, no, no. It's...

00:07:00.201 --> 00:07:02.465
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is like home to me.

00:07:02.508 --> 00:07:04.162
I have lived in a cave, though.

00:07:09.646 --> 00:07:10.995
Victoria,

00:07:11.038 --> 00:07:12.997
something about you
really makes me open up.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.955
: I feel
very comfortable talking to you.

00:07:14.999 --> 00:07:17.610
Oh, well, I think
that's enough for today.

00:07:19.612 --> 00:07:21.092
Turn it around, Lower Decks.

00:07:21.135 --> 00:07:22.615
Captain wants you in your bunks.

00:07:22.659 --> 00:07:24.530
W... Come on, man.
This is our bar.

00:07:24.574 --> 00:07:26.184
We just-we just want to grab
a drink, all right?

00:07:26.227 --> 00:07:27.315
This isn't the bar anymore.

00:07:27.359 --> 00:07:29.404
It's the commander's lounge.

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.494
And it's only for interviewees.

00:07:32.495 --> 00:07:34.148
Hey, wait,
Jet's not a commander.

00:07:34.192 --> 00:07:36.150
He's a lower decker like us.
How come he gets to be in there?

00:07:36.194 --> 00:07:37.978
There's a list
of approved people.

00:07:38.022 --> 00:07:39.414
Manhaver's on it.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:40.981
- There's a list?
- Hey, it's-it's okay.

00:07:41.025 --> 00:07:43.070
Let's get out of here.
Uh, I've got some Somnusian root

00:07:43.114 --> 00:07:44.115
that'll knock us out
for a while.

00:07:44.158 --> 00:07:45.508
I know Mom is stressed,

00:07:45.551 --> 00:07:47.161
but that reporter
is here to report.

00:07:47.205 --> 00:07:49.729
And this isn't
how the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; actually is.

00:07:49.773 --> 00:07:50.774
What are you gonna do?

00:07:50.817 --> 00:07:52.776
I'm gonna tell the truth.

00:07:58.085 --> 00:08:00.827
The very first mission
for Project Swing By.

00:08:00.871 --> 00:08:02.437
Tell me, Captain,
are you nervous?

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:04.570
The Ornarans were peaceful
when last contacted,

00:08:04.614 --> 00:08:06.354
but we should be ready
for anything.

00:08:06.398 --> 00:08:10.271
Well, I, for one, feel safe
with this amazing crew.

00:08:20.455 --> 00:08:23.067
Oh, wow. I didn't expect it
to be this nice.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.809
Seems like the Ornarans
are in a good place.

00:08:25.852 --> 00:08:27.593
But stay alert.

00:08:27.637 --> 00:08:29.726
Sometimes the dark reality
is hidden

00:08:29.769 --> 00:08:31.641
just beneath
the glossy exterior.

00:08:31.684 --> 00:08:34.382
Hey! Oh, gosh, wow. Starfleet.

00:08:34.426 --> 00:08:36.602
It is so joyous
that you've returned.

00:08:36.646 --> 00:08:38.604
I am B'Nir,
the local magistrate.

00:08:38.648 --> 00:08:39.605
Welcome back.

00:08:41.302 --> 00:08:44.436
I am Captain Carol Freeman
of the USS &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:44.479 --> 00:08:46.612
I know that
your people's first contact

00:08:46.656 --> 00:08:48.745
with the Federation
had its difficulties,

00:08:48.788 --> 00:08:50.181
- but we're here t...
- What?

00:08:50.224 --> 00:08:52.096
Oh. You're worried
that things got bad

00:08:52.139 --> 00:08:53.880
when Picard cut us off
from the felicium.

00:08:53.924 --> 00:08:55.621
Well, uh... did they?

00:08:55.665 --> 00:08:58.102
No. Picard was absolutely right.

00:08:58.145 --> 00:08:59.799
It was the best thing
that ever happened to us.

00:08:59.843 --> 00:09:01.888
Look. We even made a mural.

00:09:01.932 --> 00:09:04.151
See, there's the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt;
leaving us with no drugs,

00:09:04.195 --> 00:09:06.110
and here's all of us
freaking out.

00:09:06.153 --> 00:09:08.155
We were in a bit of a bad place
for the first, oh,

00:09:08.199 --> 00:09:09.548
ten, 14 years,

00:09:09.592 --> 00:09:11.071
but we figured it out.

00:09:11.115 --> 00:09:12.725
Once we shook
the old demons out, we focused

00:09:12.769 --> 00:09:14.684
on healthy diet and fitness.

00:09:14.727 --> 00:09:17.077
You could say
we're addicted to that now.

00:09:17.121 --> 00:09:19.950
My kind of people.

00:09:19.993 --> 00:09:21.299
How much you bench?

00:09:21.342 --> 00:09:22.648
Oh, we don't do it
for the numbers.

00:09:22.692 --> 00:09:24.128
We do it to quiet
the voices in our heads.

00:09:24.171 --> 00:09:26.043
Nice. I do 250.

00:09:26.086 --> 00:09:29.742
So, B'Nir, you have Starfleet
at your full disposal.

00:09:29.786 --> 00:09:32.397
How may we be of assistance?

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:33.485
Yeah, we're good.

00:09:33.528 --> 00:09:34.660
Well, there must be something.

00:09:34.704 --> 00:09:36.096
We have medical supplies,

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.445
engineering know-how,

00:09:37.489 --> 00:09:38.838
unlimited snacks.

00:09:38.882 --> 00:09:40.448
Starfleet's done enough
for Ornara.

00:09:40.492 --> 00:09:42.059
There's really no need
for this visit.

00:09:42.102 --> 00:09:43.800
Now, excuse me...

00:09:43.843 --> 00:09:46.150
but I'm late for my 10K.

00:09:47.499 --> 00:09:49.153
Captain, do you anticipate

00:09:49.196 --> 00:09:50.676
all Project Swing By missions
will be this...

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.417
superfluous?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.376
I'm just gonna step off imager
to make a quick call.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:56.900
Top secret Starfleet business.

00:09:56.943 --> 00:09:58.510
While we're waiting,

00:09:58.553 --> 00:10:00.686
I could tell you
about my own fitness journey.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:01.774
Cool.

00:10:01.818 --> 00:10:03.384
&lt;i&gt;Ah. Carol.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:03.428 --> 00:10:04.603
&lt;i&gt;How's the mission going?&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:04.647 --> 00:10:06.344
There is no mission.

00:10:06.387 --> 00:10:08.041
- The Ornarans don't need us. &lt;i&gt;
- That can't be right.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:08.085 --> 00:10:09.695
&lt;i&gt;Make them show you
their government,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:09.739 --> 00:10:11.828
&lt;i&gt;just in case
it's secretly run by kids&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:11.871 --> 00:10:13.351
&lt;i&gt;or somebody pretending
to be the devil...&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:13.394 --> 00:10:15.048
There's nothing funky here, Les.

00:10:15.092 --> 00:10:17.137
- Picard knew what he was doing. &lt;i&gt;
- Damn it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:17.181 --> 00:10:20.488
&lt;i&gt;We need something or the entire
program could be in jeopardy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:20.532 --> 00:10:22.403
We could go back to Beta III.

00:10:22.447 --> 00:10:24.797
There's a pretty good chance
they've fallen for Landru again.

00:10:24.841 --> 00:10:27.626
&lt;i&gt;What about the neighbors?
The pusher planet?&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.107
&lt;i&gt;Maybe they're dealing with some
difficulties that we can fix.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.284
Yes. They were left off
even worse than the Ornarans.

00:10:33.327 --> 00:10:35.678
You know, my little saying goes,
"Glutes are cute,

00:10:35.721 --> 00:10:38.637
but obliques are for freaks."

00:10:38.681 --> 00:10:40.639
Well, everything seems
in order here.

00:10:40.683 --> 00:10:43.207
So now we'll be continuing
Project Swing By

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.774
on the nearby planet Brekka.

00:10:44.817 --> 00:10:46.732
- We are?
- Just as planned.

00:10:46.776 --> 00:10:49.082
&lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; four to beam up.

00:10:57.743 --> 00:10:58.701
Yo. Newslady.

00:10:58.744 --> 00:11:00.050
Ensign Mariner,

00:11:00.093 --> 00:11:01.442
I was just about to go interview
your mother.

00:11:01.486 --> 00:11:03.053
Yeah, well, before that,
I've got some things

00:11:03.096 --> 00:11:04.141
you're going to want to hear.

00:11:04.184 --> 00:11:05.142
On the record?

00:11:05.185 --> 00:11:07.013
Well, then, come on in.

00:11:14.281 --> 00:11:16.153
Mm-hmm. Ah.

00:11:18.372 --> 00:11:19.722
Hmm.

00:11:22.986 --> 00:11:24.030
Come in.

00:11:25.553 --> 00:11:27.773
Captain Freeman, is this
a good time for our interview?

00:11:27.817 --> 00:11:30.602
Of course. Please, have a seat.

00:11:30.645 --> 00:11:32.125
Super. Shall we dive right in?

00:11:32.169 --> 00:11:34.824
I think you've seen
that I run a tight ship

00:11:34.867 --> 00:11:37.435
capable of far more
than just second contact.

00:11:37.478 --> 00:11:39.698
Actually,
after my crew interviews,

00:11:39.742 --> 00:11:42.266
"tight" isn't the word I would
use to describe the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:42.309 --> 00:11:44.181
Oh. What would you call us?

00:11:44.224 --> 00:11:46.226
Chaotic. "Irresponsible."

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.012
"Silly" is a word that has
been tossed around quite a bit.

00:11:49.055 --> 00:11:51.841
What? N-No. No, I don't know
what you've been hearing,

00:11:51.884 --> 00:11:55.105
but I can assure you,
nothing about our work is silly.

00:11:55.148 --> 00:11:58.195
Is it true that your first
officer turned into a giant head

00:11:58.238 --> 00:12:00.806
that tried to eat the ship
like a hamburger?

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.460
He... That was a one-time thing.

00:12:02.503 --> 00:12:04.375
It was a strange
energies situation--

00:12:04.418 --> 00:12:06.681
something that many other crews
have had to deal with as well.

00:12:06.725 --> 00:12:08.901
I also hear you left your post
to take some engineers

00:12:08.945 --> 00:12:10.555
on a spa trip, where you had

00:12:10.598 --> 00:12:12.557
an emotional breakdown.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.167
Who told you that?

00:12:14.211 --> 00:12:16.387
Did you or did you not
transport a Doopler

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:17.823
into a Starfleet party

00:12:17.867 --> 00:12:19.564
as revenge
for not being allowed inside?

00:12:19.607 --> 00:12:21.392
If you had been there,
you would have...

00:12:21.435 --> 00:12:23.350
And tell me, Captain, was
that the same vindictive streak

00:12:23.394 --> 00:12:26.266
that led you to purposely give
a Pandronian drill instructor

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.225
- a poly-heart attack?
- Uh-uh-uh, she was...

00:12:28.268 --> 00:12:29.922
Your head of security
was turned into a puppet,

00:12:29.966 --> 00:12:31.315
you let spear-wielding aliens

00:12:31.358 --> 00:12:32.925
take over the ship,
you got Quark kidnapped,

00:12:32.969 --> 00:12:34.535
then there was the whole thing
with the exocomp,

00:12:34.579 --> 00:12:37.016
and I'm seeing
a lot of stuff about Q.

00:12:38.626 --> 00:12:39.932
Okay. Look alive, people.

00:12:39.976 --> 00:12:42.108
Everybody's favorite ensign
on deck.

00:12:42.152 --> 00:12:43.936
Uh, Captain wanted to see me?

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:45.808
Yeesh. Tough crowd.

00:12:45.851 --> 00:12:48.288
I guess the camera
really does add ten frowns.

00:12:48.332 --> 00:12:49.376
You know?

00:12:50.987 --> 00:12:54.251
Okay, I don't usually worry
about morale,

00:12:54.294 --> 00:12:56.035
but the energy out there
is dark.

00:12:56.079 --> 00:12:57.907
I think everybody's on edge
about the reporter.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.997
Mariner... [sighs] I saw you
go into Victoria's quarters.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.042
What the hell
did you say to her?!

00:13:03.086 --> 00:13:04.435
I know.
I wasn't on the list, okay?

00:13:04.478 --> 00:13:06.089
But I had to tell her
some stories,

00:13:06.132 --> 00:13:07.873
you know, about what
it's really like to work here.

00:13:07.917 --> 00:13:10.789
So you went out of your way
to make me look like a fool.

00:13:10.833 --> 00:13:12.138
I just told her the truth.

00:13:12.182 --> 00:13:13.879
You went too far
this time, Mariner.

00:13:13.923 --> 00:13:16.751
You told her all sorts
of terrible, out-of-context...

00:13:16.795 --> 00:13:18.101
I gave context.

00:13:18.144 --> 00:13:19.929
When are you gonna
grow up, Beckett?

00:13:19.972 --> 00:13:23.019
You have absolutely no concept
of when to shut your mouth.

00:13:23.062 --> 00:13:24.585
Don't talk to me like I'm 15.

00:13:24.629 --> 00:13:25.935
I'm a Starfleet officer

00:13:25.978 --> 00:13:27.588
and an essential part
of your crew.

00:13:27.632 --> 00:13:28.981
Not anymore.

00:13:29.025 --> 00:13:30.809
What is-what is that
supposed to mean?

00:13:30.853 --> 00:13:32.115
Uh, Captain, what are you doing?

00:13:32.158 --> 00:13:34.160
Oh, you want
to backstab, complain

00:13:34.204 --> 00:13:35.901
and be hard to work with?

00:13:35.945 --> 00:13:37.772
Well, there's a place
for people like that.

00:13:37.816 --> 00:13:39.905
It's called Starbase 80.

00:13:39.949 --> 00:13:40.906
Starbase 80?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.125
What about it?

00:13:42.168 --> 00:13:43.343
I've already put through
the transfer.

00:13:43.387 --> 00:13:44.910
Shuttle's on the way.

00:13:44.954 --> 00:13:46.607
Mom, is-is this a joke?
Where's the hover-cam?

00:13:46.651 --> 00:13:48.087
Does it look like I'm joking?

00:13:48.131 --> 00:13:50.568
I want you off of my ship
before we get to Brekka

00:13:50.611 --> 00:13:52.439
so you don't cause
any more damage.

00:13:52.483 --> 00:13:53.832
Oh, my God, you're not kidding.

00:13:53.876 --> 00:13:55.138
Mom, please.

00:13:55.181 --> 00:13:57.880
You are no longer
my ensign or my problem.

00:13:57.923 --> 00:14:00.360
I don't even know if I can
call you my daughter anymore.

00:14:00.404 --> 00:14:01.622
Dismissed.

00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:10.631
Made us sound like losers.

00:14:10.675 --> 00:14:12.111
Yeah. Starbase 80.

00:14:12.155 --> 00:14:14.244
- Hey, Mariner...
- Levy, I can't right now.

00:14:14.287 --> 00:14:15.854
I know that this is all part
of some temporal

00:14:15.898 --> 00:14:17.464
cold war shenanigans,

00:14:17.508 --> 00:14:20.685
but what you did
is really messed up.

00:14:20.728 --> 00:14:22.208
Oh, Jennifer.

00:14:22.252 --> 00:14:23.688
My mom is acting like

00:14:23.731 --> 00:14:25.255
I stabbed her in the back,
and I need...

00:14:25.298 --> 00:14:26.734
We're all trying to put
our best foot forward.

00:14:26.778 --> 00:14:28.998
Ugh, what you did
hurt the entire crew.

00:14:29.041 --> 00:14:30.521
Well, I didn't-I didn't
do anything.

00:14:30.564 --> 00:14:31.914
T-Tell me what I did.

00:14:31.957 --> 00:14:33.393
I'm gonna keep my opinions
to myself.

00:14:33.437 --> 00:14:34.786
You should try it.

00:14:34.829 --> 00:14:36.483
Here, you can
have your candle back,

00:14:36.527 --> 00:14:37.658
since it clearly
didn't mean anything.

00:14:37.702 --> 00:14:38.964
I feel like I'm going crazy.

00:14:39.008 --> 00:14:40.574
I'm-I'm losing my mind.

00:14:40.618 --> 00:14:42.228
Is this a-is this
a &lt;i&gt;Frame of Mind&lt;/i&gt; thing?

00:14:42.272 --> 00:14:43.751
Am I gonna wake up
with a neural drain on my head?

00:14:43.795 --> 00:14:45.928
The only neural drain
around here is you.

00:14:45.971 --> 00:14:47.755
Jennifer, I need you
to believe me.

00:14:47.799 --> 00:14:49.366
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:14:49.409 --> 00:14:51.020
How am I supposed to trust you?

00:14:51.063 --> 00:14:53.544
You tell everyone all the time
this is who you are.

00:14:53.587 --> 00:14:54.980
Yeah, but you know me better
than that.

00:14:55.024 --> 00:14:56.677
I really don't.

00:14:56.721 --> 00:14:58.505
- &lt;i&gt;
- Attention, all crew.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:58.549 --> 00:14:59.985
&lt;i&gt;For operational security,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:00.029 --> 00:15:01.682
&lt;i&gt;please refrain
from communicating&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:01.726 --> 00:15:04.598
&lt;i&gt;with former&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;officer Mariner.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:05.948 --> 00:15:07.427
Give the stupid candle
to Castro.

00:15:07.471 --> 00:15:08.602
I don't care.

00:15:14.478 --> 00:15:16.088
- Mariner, we just heard.
- You're being transferred?

00:15:16.132 --> 00:15:18.525
Apparently I torpedoed
the whole California-class.

00:15:18.569 --> 00:15:20.875
You've done a lot worse
than this. It's gonna blow over.

00:15:20.919 --> 00:15:21.876
I didn't do anything.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.095
Oh, yeah, no, sure.

00:15:23.139 --> 00:15:24.705
But maybe just apologize

00:15:24.749 --> 00:15:26.838
- for what she thinks you did?
- Ugh, whatever.

00:15:26.881 --> 00:15:28.709
It's not my first time
getting kicked off a ship.

00:15:28.753 --> 00:15:30.842
You know, the goodbyes are
the worst part, so let's just...

00:15:30.885 --> 00:15:32.278
Let's not say anything.

00:15:33.932 --> 00:15:36.195
Mariner, you-you can't leave
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:36.239 --> 00:15:37.283
Yeah, I can.

00:15:37.327 --> 00:15:39.503
This always happens.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.251
You lost it, man.

00:15:48.294 --> 00:15:50.818
No, I didn't lose it.
It's around here somewhere.

00:15:50.862 --> 00:15:53.125
Oh, hey.
You Ensign Bucket Mariner?

00:15:53.169 --> 00:15:54.387
Beckett. Yeah.

00:15:54.431 --> 00:15:56.041
Oh, Beckett. Right.

00:15:56.085 --> 00:15:58.348
Must've got some elbow grease
on this thing.

00:15:58.391 --> 00:15:59.784
That's not what elbow grease is.

00:15:59.827 --> 00:16:02.308
Ooh, this is a nice ship.

00:16:02.352 --> 00:16:05.007
Doesn't smell
like garbage &lt;i&gt;or&lt;/i&gt; sweat.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.096
Man, I'd do anything
to work here.

00:16:07.139 --> 00:16:09.750
So, Captain coming
to see you off or what?

00:16:09.794 --> 00:16:11.143
Guess not.

00:16:11.187 --> 00:16:13.667
All right, I'm transferred.
Let's go.

00:16:13.711 --> 00:16:16.583
Here's your uniform.
It's, uh, one-size-fits-some.

00:16:19.108 --> 00:16:20.761
Oh, my sammich!

00:16:20.805 --> 00:16:22.111
Ah. See?

00:16:22.154 --> 00:16:23.416
Told you I didn't eat it.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.505
- Mmm.
- Oh.

00:16:40.042 --> 00:16:41.608
Orders, Captain?

00:16:41.652 --> 00:16:42.783
Resume course.

00:16:58.582 --> 00:17:00.279
&lt;i&gt;Captain,
we are in orbit of Brekka.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:00.323 --> 00:17:02.977
Dr. Migleemo, you have the conn.

00:17:03.021 --> 00:17:05.415
Ba-ha-ha.
A feast of opportunities

00:17:05.458 --> 00:17:06.764
to make you proud, Captain.

00:17:06.807 --> 00:17:08.809
Keep it together, Doctor.
You'll do fine.

00:17:09.767 --> 00:17:12.161
It's really happening.

00:17:12.204 --> 00:17:13.901
- Orders, sir?
- Yes.

00:17:13.945 --> 00:17:16.774
Initiate a subspace
communication link to my meema.

00:17:16.817 --> 00:17:19.559
I want her to see her
special boy being the captain!

00:17:19.603 --> 00:17:21.561
Yes, sir.

00:17:25.261 --> 00:17:27.176
Well, I hope you know
my daughter's stories

00:17:27.219 --> 00:17:28.351
are heavily biased.

00:17:28.394 --> 00:17:29.874
Oh, is that so?

00:17:29.917 --> 00:17:32.224
Your focus should be
with Project Swing By

00:17:32.268 --> 00:17:33.530
and the benefit it can have

00:17:33.573 --> 00:17:35.271
to the forgotten planets
in the quadrant.

00:17:35.314 --> 00:17:37.186
Well, that remains to be seen.

00:17:37.229 --> 00:17:38.883
Perhaps you'll be able
to help more here on Brekka,

00:17:38.926 --> 00:17:41.146
because, frankly,
Ornara was a dud.

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:44.018
I'm sure we're
about to be extremely useful.

00:17:44.062 --> 00:17:46.325
Uh, useful to whom, exactly?

00:17:46.369 --> 00:17:49.154
Well, good thing
Starfleet is here

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:50.590
to notice that
everyone is missing.

00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:53.027
Project Swing By
seems like a success.

00:17:55.029 --> 00:17:57.815
Phasers out.
Something's not right.

00:18:03.342 --> 00:18:04.343
Oh.

00:18:04.387 --> 00:18:06.345
Hello. Captain, I found someone.

00:18:07.433 --> 00:18:08.652
:
Please, you have to go.

00:18:08.695 --> 00:18:10.306
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:18:10.349 --> 00:18:11.611
I'm with Starfleet. I can help.
Where is everyone?

00:18:11.655 --> 00:18:13.483
Aah!

00:18:13.526 --> 00:18:14.484
No!

00:18:15.702 --> 00:18:17.400
Breen?

00:18:17.443 --> 00:18:21.273
Aah! Captain, there are
Breen soldiers in the city.

00:18:21.317 --> 00:18:23.754
Aah!
We need to evacuate. Ow!

00:18:27.758 --> 00:18:28.802
Stay down!

00:18:28.846 --> 00:18:30.195
In a stunning development,

00:18:30.239 --> 00:18:32.589
Breen soldiers
have occupied Brekka!

00:18:32.632 --> 00:18:34.199
Not since the Dominion War
have I...

00:18:34.243 --> 00:18:35.592
Aah!

00:18:35.635 --> 00:18:37.463
Emergency transport now.

00:18:40.945 --> 00:18:43.252
Red alert.
All hands to battle sta...

00:18:43.295 --> 00:18:44.949
Meema?

00:18:44.992 --> 00:18:46.429
Uh, M-Mother, you should not
be calling me at work.

00:18:46.472 --> 00:18:48.082
- Goodbye.
- Mr. Boimler,

00:18:48.126 --> 00:18:50.041
I need some distance
between us and this system.

00:18:50.084 --> 00:18:51.738
Breen interceptors closing fast.

00:18:51.782 --> 00:18:53.479
They're firing!

00:18:53.523 --> 00:18:54.654
Oh!

00:19:06.231 --> 00:19:07.276
Shields are failing!

00:19:09.756 --> 00:19:10.714
&lt;i&gt;Fire torpedoes!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:10.757 --> 00:19:11.889
Full spread!

00:19:15.849 --> 00:19:17.808
&lt;i&gt;They covered
the spread, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:17.851 --> 00:19:19.157
Aah!
Shields are down.

00:19:22.247 --> 00:19:23.205
Brace for impact!

00:19:27.252 --> 00:19:28.253
Damage to all decks.

00:19:28.297 --> 00:19:30.081
Seal affected areas.

00:19:34.564 --> 00:19:36.261
Captain, we're being hailed.

00:19:38.307 --> 00:19:40.352
Why aren't they
finishing us off?

00:19:43.312 --> 00:19:44.748
They're going to board us.

00:19:44.791 --> 00:19:46.619
All hands,
prepare countermeasures.

00:19:58.892 --> 00:20:00.633
The Breen don't take prisoners.

00:20:00.677 --> 00:20:02.156
Do not try to negotiate.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.115
Defend yourselves at all costs.

00:20:04.158 --> 00:20:05.812
- Captain, incoming ship.
- More Breen?

00:20:05.856 --> 00:20:06.900
No, it's, uh...

00:20:06.944 --> 00:20:08.032
I think it's Starfleet.

00:20:13.777 --> 00:20:15.431
What the hell
kind of ship is that?

00:20:33.927 --> 00:20:34.972
They're gonna ram us!

00:20:45.939 --> 00:20:47.071
Hail that vessel.

00:20:47.114 --> 00:20:48.333
I want to know who to thank

00:20:48.377 --> 00:20:50.248
for saving our lives.

00:20:50.292 --> 00:20:52.946
Captain, there are no life signs
aboard that ship.

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:54.600
What?

00:20:54.644 --> 00:20:55.862
Uh, incoming communication
from Admiral Buenamigo.

00:20:55.906 --> 00:20:57.516
Main screen.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:59.475
&lt;i&gt;Carol,
thank goodness you're okay.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:59.518 --> 00:21:01.477
&lt;i&gt;We tried to get here
as soon as possible.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.957
Les, wh...
Are you on that ship?

00:21:04.001 --> 00:21:06.873
&lt;i&gt;No one is.
Meet the new Texas-class.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:06.917 --> 00:21:08.832
&lt;i&gt;This is the&lt;/i&gt; Aledo,

00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:12.357
&lt;i&gt;the first of three fully
automated Federation starships.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:12.401 --> 00:21:15.447
&lt;i&gt;And it looks like
she just passed her sea trials.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:15.491 --> 00:21:18.363
Admiral, wow,
this ship is amazing.

00:21:18.407 --> 00:21:20.844
&lt;i&gt;As of today,
consider it declassified.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:20.887 --> 00:21:23.020
&lt;i&gt;I'm happy to tell you
anything and everything&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:23.063 --> 00:21:24.630
&lt;i&gt;about the Texas-class.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:24.674 --> 00:21:26.240
&lt;i&gt;See, our goal
for this new class of ship&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:26.284 --> 00:21:27.981
&lt;i&gt;- was to remove the...&lt;/i&gt;
- What the [bleep] just happened?

00:21:28.025 --> 00:21:29.853
I don't know, Captain.
But Project Swing By

00:21:29.896 --> 00:21:31.376
just revealed a Breen incursion,

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.727
so I think everyone's
gonna be very impressed.

00:21:37.643 --> 00:21:39.471
In my time on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:39.515 --> 00:21:42.822
I experienced a culture
of conflict between the crew.

00:21:42.866 --> 00:21:44.563
I mean, Ops is clearly the best.

00:21:44.607 --> 00:21:47.349
We never had to take
a spa vacation like Engineering.

00:21:47.392 --> 00:21:49.176
The captain totally lost it,
by the way.

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.135
Those engineers
are so hard to deal with.

00:21:51.178 --> 00:21:53.442
I got turned into a puppet
on my very first mission.

00:21:53.485 --> 00:21:55.531
Uh, the crew never
held it against me, though.

00:21:55.574 --> 00:21:57.446
Oh, you should have
heard Quark scream

00:21:57.489 --> 00:21:59.404
when he was being carried away.

00:21:59.448 --> 00:22:02.059
"Aah!"

00:22:02.102 --> 00:22:03.756
I-I'm sorry.
What was the question again?

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.977
Although there were some
who had nothing but praise.

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:08.544
Well, there's the family
you're born into, right,

00:22:08.587 --> 00:22:09.980
and then the family you choose.

00:22:10.023 --> 00:22:11.547
I've got both here
on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:13.026
If you're measuring by heart,

00:22:13.070 --> 00:22:14.637
this is the strongest ship
in the fleet.

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:17.074
Because we've got
the best captain at the helm,

00:22:17.117 --> 00:22:19.119
- my mom.
- But this sole voice

00:22:19.163 --> 00:22:20.730
of California-class
exceptionalism

00:22:20.773 --> 00:22:22.384
was transferred off the ship

00:22:22.427 --> 00:22:24.603
&lt;i&gt;just for talking to me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:24.647 --> 00:22:26.910
&lt;i&gt;Is Freeman
really the best captain&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:26.953 --> 00:22:29.956
&lt;i&gt;or simply a cruel taskmaster?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.481
&lt;i&gt;I'm Victoria Nuzé for FNN.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:32.524 --> 00:22:33.525
Mariner didn't say anything bad
about the ship.

00:22:33.569 --> 00:22:34.526
It was everybody else.

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:35.701
They didn't even realize

00:22:35.745 --> 00:22:36.963
what they were doing.

00:22:37.007 --> 00:22:38.400
I knew something was off.

00:22:38.443 --> 00:22:39.879
We should have made her stay.

00:22:39.923 --> 00:22:41.838
I can't imagine
how the captain's feeling.

00:22:43.492 --> 00:22:45.058
Ugh, come on, come on.

00:22:45.102 --> 00:22:48.018
&lt;i&gt;Hey-o. Starbase 80.
What do you need?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:48.061 --> 00:22:49.759
This is Captain Carol Freeman.

00:22:49.802 --> 00:22:51.587
I've made a terrible mistake.

00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:53.937
I need to speak
with Ensign Beckett Mariner.

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.678
&lt;i&gt;- Who? Hold on.
- Oh, no, you don't!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:55.721 --> 00:22:56.896
Would you just use

00:22:56.940 --> 00:22:58.855
&lt;i&gt;the freakin' broom already?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:58.898 --> 00:23:01.379
&lt;i&gt;Uh, sorry. We got a Pyrithian
bat flying around in here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:01.423 --> 00:23:02.685
What the [bleep]?

00:23:02.728 --> 00:23:03.903
&lt;i&gt;I said hit it with the broom.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:03.947 --> 00:23:05.818
&lt;i&gt;I did that. It didn't care.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:05.862 --> 00:23:07.472
Ensign Beckett Mariner.

00:23:07.516 --> 00:23:09.300
Can you please just connect me?

00:23:09.343 --> 00:23:10.606
&lt;i&gt;All right, calm down, lady.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:10.649 --> 00:23:11.868
&lt;i&gt;You ain't&lt;/i&gt; my &lt;i&gt;captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:11.911 --> 00:23:13.173
&lt;i&gt;Let's see, let's see.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:13.217 --> 00:23:14.784
&lt;i&gt;Marner, Marner.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:14.827 --> 00:23:17.134
&lt;i&gt;Oh, yeah. Nope.
Can't connect you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:17.177 --> 00:23:19.049
You don't even have
working communications?

00:23:19.092 --> 00:23:20.964
&lt;i&gt;Rude. Of course we do. Usually.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:21.007 --> 00:23:22.618
&lt;i&gt;But this one here resigned.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:22.661 --> 00:23:23.662
Resigned? What?

00:23:23.706 --> 00:23:25.447
No. Are you sure?

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.710
&lt;i&gt;Yep. Handed in her combadge
and phaser and...&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:27.753 --> 00:23:29.407
&lt;i&gt;- ! Hit it. Hit it.
- Look out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:29.451 --> 00:23:30.669
&lt;i&gt;Hit the bat.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:31.365 --> 00:23:33.367
What have I done?

00:23:33.411 --> 00:23:36.632
Oh, Beckett. Where are you?

00:23:45.554 --> 00:23:47.817
Hey, so I just got a hot tip
on some Vedalan mummies.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.297
Should be pretty ancient.

00:23:50.341 --> 00:23:52.299
Want to check 'em out,
Number One?

00:23:52.343 --> 00:23:54.214
Eh, they're not gonna dig up
themselves, right?

00:23:54.258 --> 00:23:56.086
Because that would be,
like, very unsettling.

00:23:56.129 --> 00:23:58.305
No. I mean,
once or twice, they have.

00:23:58.349 --> 00:23:59.829
But, nah, odds are they won't.

00:23:59.872 --> 00:24:02.701
Then hell yeah.
Let's mummy it up.

00:25:07.766 --> 00:25:11.766
Chirp.
